%% Interview-mode turn and debrief.
%% Sources: CONTEXT.md (interview mode, memory), ADR-0004 (code decides the flow), ADR-0005 (memory).
sequenceDiagram
    actor C as Candidate
    box rgb(243,244,246) Planned M3
        participant G as Interview graph
        participant Q as Question card
        participant I as Interviewer, GLM-5.3
        participant F as Grader, GLM-5.3-Flash
    end
    box rgb(243,244,246) Planned M4
        participant S as Memory, SQLite store
    end

    Note over C,S: Legend: grey box planned with its milestone. Nothing here is built yet, the walking skeleton has no interview mode.
    C->>G: /interview, then choose a track
    G->>Q: load a question card for the track
    Q-->>G: question, level anchors, rubric checks, probes
    G->>I: phrase the opening question
    I-->>G: question text
    G-->>C: opening question, graph waits on an interrupt
    loop until deep enough, stuck, or the budget is spent
        alt candidate answers
            C->>G: answer
            G->>F: grade yes or no per rubric check, with a quote
            F-->>G: verdicts, new correct content, says they do not know
            Note over G: plain-code policy picks probe, hint, move on or stop
            G->>I: phrase the next probe or question
            I-->>G: question text
            G-->>C: probe or next question
        else candidate types /hint
            C->>G: /hint
            G->>G: climb the hint ladder for this skill
            Note over G: record the hint used, it caps this skill's level
            G-->>C: next hint, from a nudge down to the answer itself
        end
    end
    Note over C,F: the session ends and the debrief starts
    par one isolated grader call per rubric check, fanned out with Send
        G->>F: rubric check 1
    and
        G->>F: rubric check n
    end
    F-->>G: final verdicts with quotes
    G->>G: level roll-up in plain code, capped by hints used
    G-->>C: debrief with verdicts, level, hints used, gaps, reference answer
    G->>S: deferred write after the debrief is shown, session record and candidate model
    Note over F,S: the grader never receives memory
